1
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:06,047
ACR is the Arc Compute Rate:

2
00:00:06,087 --> 00:00:08,300
a reference rate for machine commerce.

3
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:11,005
It brings compute benchmarks, billing evidence,

4
00:00:11,045 --> 00:00:14,506
and on-chain infrastructure into one place.

5
00:00:14,956 --> 00:00:18,898
Here are its inference, GPU, and data indices.

6
00:00:18,938 --> 00:00:21,789
Aomi helps users investigate compute bills using

7
00:00:21,829 --> 00:00:25,040
ACR’s evidence and public price comparisons.

8
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,421
Evidence age matters,

9
00:00:26,461 --> 00:00:29,563
and a benchmark never authorizes payment.

10
00:00:30,013 --> 00:00:32,690
This is more than an API integration.

11
00:00:32,730 --> 00:00:36,219
ACR has an on-chain oracle, attestations,

12
00:00:36,259 --> 00:00:38,351
and settlement infrastructure.

13
00:00:38,442 --> 00:00:40,445
Aomi connects protocol-specific

14
00:00:40,485 --> 00:00:42,547
knowledge and off-chain records

15
00:00:42,587 --> 00:00:46,709
to a harness that can prepare reviewed contract actions.

16
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:48,223
For treasury payments,

17
00:00:48,263 --> 00:00:50,812
the recorded bill determines the recipient,

18
00:00:50,852 --> 00:00:53,575
amount, category, and decision hash.

19
00:00:53,615 --> 00:00:56,605
Aomi stages spendAsOwner, simulates it,

20
00:00:56,645 --> 00:00:58,846
and requests owner authorization.

21
00:00:58,886 --> 00:01:01,586
The guard restricts chain, contract, and function;

22
00:01:01,626 --> 00:01:03,780
PolicyWallet enforces ownership,

23
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:06,643
budget, and replay protection.

24
00:01:07,093 --> 00:01:10,884
After payment, ACR verifies the successful receipt and

25
00:01:10,924 --> 00:01:13,984
matching event before reconciling the original bill.

26
00:01:14,024 --> 00:01:16,562
That closes the loop: off-chain evidence,

27
00:01:16,602 --> 00:01:18,408
authorized on-chain action,

28
00:01:18,448 --> 00:01:21,421
and a business record that knows what settled.

29
00:01:21,872 --> 00:01:25,454
Back in the product, Ask ACR Agent is the entry point.

30
00:01:25,494 --> 00:01:28,194
The merged frontend imports Aomi’s widget

31
00:01:28,234 --> 00:01:30,957
and pins it to the hosted ACR app.

32
00:01:30,997 --> 00:01:32,966
The protocol keeps its own interface;

33
00:01:33,006 --> 00:01:35,875
the component supplies the conversation.

34
00:01:36,325 --> 00:01:39,617
That is the foundation for one-shotting a protocol app.

35
00:01:39,657 --> 00:01:41,951
Describe the workflow, connect the infrastructure,

36
00:01:41,991 --> 00:01:44,760
and define the contract actions and guards.

37
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:47,501
Aomi supplies the agent runtime and frontend

38
00:01:47,541 --> 00:01:50,700
component around those protocol-specific pieces.

39
00:01:51,150 --> 00:01:53,339
The frontend integration is shipped.

40
00:01:53,379 --> 00:01:55,777
The treasury workflow is implemented,

41
00:01:55,817 --> 00:01:58,273
with production payment acceptance still pending.

42
00:01:58,313 --> 00:02:00,642
The value is one agent that connects

43
00:02:00,682 --> 00:02:03,899
understanding the protocol with acting on it.
